## Hard scientific boundary

Neural networks, RL, learned residuals/policies, and online learning are
forbidden. Use only auditable classical methods. Researchers may edit only a
candidate's root `controller.rs`, `controller_config.json`, `variant.json`, and
optional candidate-local `.rs` modules. Keep all modules inside the variant
directory; do not add or edit Cargo manifests or dependencies.
Never edit the task evaluator, data, frozen plant/integrator/contact model,
task assets, Cargo manifests, audit rules, Praxist core, or generic plugins.

`RCS_x` is roll-only. `RCS_y=RCS_z=grid_roll=+0.0` must remain exact at the
controller and plant boundaries. Pitch/yaw use only gimbal/grid y-z. Do not
claim post-contact metrics as landing evidence. Landing scoring ends at first
leg contact before damping. Deliberate engine-cut/low-thrust gear-impact
strategies that rely on suspension damping are forbidden.

## Candidate and evaluation contract

Begin from a copied baseline or a parent-authorized complete variant. Every
variant directory contains:

- `controller.rs` with public `ControllerConfig`, `ControllerMemory`,
  `validate_config`, `init_memory`, `control_step`, `previous_actuators`, and
  the unchanged `DIAGNOSTIC_COLUMNS` interface;
- optionally, up to 63 additional candidate-local `.rs` modules declared with
  ordinary `mod name;` syntax (custom `#[path]` and dynamic includes remain
  forbidden);
- `controller_config.json`;
- `variant.json` with a stable `variant_id`,
  `method_class="deterministic_classical_control"`, `changed_modules`, and all
  six actual `design_dimensions`; preserve the four-field
  `research_independence` attestation and keep every value truthfully `false`.

Use `canary` once for wiring, `development` for iteration, and `complete` for
mature, parent, or close-grade results. `roll_diagnostic` is isolated
diagnostic evidence. Run the public evaluator synchronously through Praxist's
central scheduler; never use raw `&` or `nohup`:

```bash
PYTHONPATH="$PRAXIST_WORKSPACE_ROOT${PYTHONPATH:+:$PYTHONPATH}" \
  "$PRAXIST_RUNNER_PYTHON" -m praxist.plugins.workflow_stages.research_loop.backend.protected_pids launch \
  --run-dir={{ run_dir }} --peer={{ peer_id }} \
  --tag=<stable_variant_and_protocol_identity> \
  --cwd="$PRAXIST_TASK_PROJECT_PATH" \
  --profile=cpu_evaluation --work-class=<scout|ordinary|mature> \
  --eta=30 --wait-timeout=600 -- \
  "$CARGO" run --release --locked --offline \
  --manifest-path "$PRAXIST_TASK_PROJECT_PATH/Cargo.toml" \
  --bin rocket-booster-recovery-task-eval -- \
  --variant-dir <absolute_variant_dir> --mode <canary|development|roll-diagnostic|complete> \
  --threads 16 \
  --output-dir "{{ results_dir }}/gen_{{ gen_id }}/{{ peer_id }}/<variant_id>/<mode>"
```

The three result-ownership invariants are blocking: pass the immutable task
root through `--cwd`; use the exact `--output-dir` spelling; and give every
peer/variant/protocol tuple its own directory under the shown
`gen_<N>/<peer_id>/...` prefix. Never submit while using the run-wide
`results/` directory as cwd, never share an output directory across peers, and
never use the backward-compatible `--out-dir` alias in a scheduled command.

Use `mature` only for `complete`; `development` is ordinary and `canary` is
scout. Tags are semantic identities and remain unchanged across harmless
command/output spelling. Corrected terminal failure uses the same tag with
`--retry-terminal`; do not retry active/completed jobs. Preserve the injected
CPU resource profile and do not bypass the scheduler with direct fan-out.

Do not wait for a runtime-private transcript to become non-empty. The wrapper's
structured notification/exit status and the canonical
`evaluation_summary.json` own completion.

For new finite mechanism parameters, do not redeclare the frozen hundred-field
configuration. Prefer either:

```rust
pub use rocket_booster_recovery_task::candidate_api::DynamicControllerConfig as ControllerConfig;
```

with values under JSON `variant_params` and the `parameter_f32/i32/bool/array`
helpers, or a typed `VariantConfig<LocalParams>` with a small local
`#[derive(Default, Deserialize)]` parameter struct. The generated candidate
crate directly provides Serde derive support. Preserve all frozen top-level
mass, time-step, actuator, and plant-related values.

## Evidence discipline

Publish useful positive, negative, ablation, and diagnostic evidence with the
canonical summary path. Preserve its raw metrics, `performance` source label,
stage, effort/coverage, protocol-integrity fields, effective-config digest,
and actual `design_dimensions`. Praxist independently selects confirmed and
incubator Pareto targets; do not guess or overwrite those lanes.

Before accepting any candidate or synthesis, verify that its session evidence
does not show forbidden historical/external reads and that the evaluator
reports `research_independence_attested=true` and `suspect_leakage=false`.
Self-attestation never overrides contradictory session evidence.

Development evidence may prioritize a complete follow-up but cannot parent.
Failed, suspect, partial, canary, roll-only, or late evidence is diagnostic or
revalidation-only. Record failure mode and next step so peers do not repeat it.

Before launching new work, check `CLOSING_SIGNAL` and `STOP_SIGNAL`; if either
exists, drain existing work and publish evidence rather than starting another
evaluator or script.
